  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Update Volunteer Status

  Updates the review status of a volunteer registration record. Used to accept, reject, or reset a volunteer application to pending. On status change, all related cache entries (single record and paginated lists) are invalidated.

  ## Authorization
  Requires `update` permission.

  ## Path Parameters

  | Parameter | Type   | Required | Description                                |
  |-----------|--------|----------|--------------------------------------------|
  | id        | string | Yes      | UUID of the volunteer registration record  |

  ## Query Parameters

  | Parameter | Type   | Required | Default   | Description / Allowed Values                  |
  |-----------|--------|----------|-----------|-----------------------------------------------|
  | status    | string | No       | `pending` | One of: `accepted`, `rejected`, `pending`     |

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`** — Returns the updated volunteer record with `id` and `status` fields.

  ## Errors

  | Status                      | Description                                             |
  |-----------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
  | `400 Bad Request`           | Invalid `id` format or unknown `status` value.          |
  | `401 Unauthorized`          | Missing or invalid authentication token.                |
  | `403 Forbidden`             | User does not have `update` permission.                 |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.                                |
}
